	"nodes":[
		{"id":"0f81adfe2c8ac4a7","type":"text","text":"file system commands\n","x":-620,"y":-80,"width":337,"height":55},
		{"id":"64a1a465d216cae5","type":"text","text":"## find\n\n```\nfind [-H] [-L] [-P] [-D debugopts] [-Olevel] [starting-point...] [expression]\n```\n\n### Options\n\n-P      Never  follow  symbolic  links.\n-L       Follow symbolic links.\n-H       Do not follow symbolic links, except while processing  the command  line  arguments.\n-D debugopts       Print  diagnostic information; this can be helpful to diagnose problems with why **find** is not doing what you want.\n-d     A synonym for -depth, for compatibility with FreeBSD, NetBSD, MacOS X and OpenBSD.\n\n## Example\n- Search for files in your home directory which have been modified in the last twenty-four hours.\n```\nfind $HOME -mtime 0 \n```\n\n- Search for files which are executable but not readable.\n```\nfind /sbin /usr/sbin  -executable \\! -readable -print\n```","x":-1360,"y":-488,"width":580,"height":872},
		{"id":"d8137ace142ab219","type":"text","text":"Linux","x":-80,"y":-82,"width":200,"height":60}
	],
